From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: ROG5 PCON follow-ups: bpc floor yields to a ceiling, D0 result, async MSA marked experimental

Follow-ups to 0119 from the GPT-6.1-Sol review (2026-10-01):

 - The 8 bpc floor for TMDS converters (and msm.dp_min_bpc) overrode a
   lower ceiling: an 18 bpp EDID or msm.dp_max_bpc=6 became 24 bpp. A
   ceiling now wins over the floor, as before the floor existed.
 - msm_dp_aux_link_power_up() returned 0 even when every D0 write failed,
   so the 0119 "sink D3 -> D0 (rc=0)" line could not report a failure. It
   now returns the AUX error, or -EIO for a short write (callers only log).
 - msm.dp_async_msa keeps static M/N; in asynchronous mode the source is
   expected to send measured M (amdgpu enables M measurement). Say that it
   is an incomplete experiment in the comment and the parameter text.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -394,10 +394,13 @@
  * (mainline and stock msm-5.4), 1 = asynchronous: CONFIGURATION_CTRL
  * SYNC_ASYNC_CLK and MISC0 bit 0 clear, TU start delay with the async margin;
  * MVID/NVID stay software-programmed (static). Applied at the next modeset.
+ * EXPERIMENTAL and incomplete: in asynchronous mode the source should send
+ * measured M values (amdgpu enables M measurement); static M/N are only
+ * clock-recovery hints. A picture proves the lead, not compliance.
  */
 static uint msm_dp_async_msa;
 module_param_named(dp_async_msa, msm_dp_async_msa, uint, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_async_msa, "ROG5: 1 = asynchronous MSA clock signalling at the next modeset (0 = synchronous)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_async_msa, "ROG5 EXPERIMENT (static M/N, not spec-complete): 1 = asynchronous MSA clock signalling at the next modeset (0 = synchronous)");
 
 static void msm_dp_ctrl_config_ctrl(struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl)
 {
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_link.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_link.c
@@ -73,7 +73,8 @@
 			break;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	/* ROG5: report a sink that never took D0 (this returned 0 regardless) */
+	return len == 1 ? 0 : (len < 0 ? len : -EIO);
 }
 
 static int msm_dp_aux_link_power_down(struct drm_dp_aux *aux,
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -300,8 +300,12 @@
 	link_info = &msm_dp_panel->link_info;
 	data_rate_khz = link_info->num_lanes * link_info->rate * 8;
 
+	/*
+	 * The floor never overrides a ceiling (EDID, downstream port,
+	 * dp_max_bpc): below it the ceiling wins, as before the floor existed.
+	 */
 	if (bpp < min_supported_bpp)
-		bpp = min_supported_bpp;
+		min_supported_bpp = bpp;
 
 	do {
 		if (mode_pclk_khz * bpp <= data_rate_khz)
